  "audit_finding_multi_target": "v2.0 MTLLadder/MTLMultiproof hash interior nodes as H(node, l, r) with no ladder/position prefix. Single-structure second preimage is 2^-n per query either way (first-run reading of a log2(depth) loss was a per-trial/per-query mis-accounting, corrected). But in the multi-target game over T \u2248 2^40 signed nodes across all zones, one evaluation is tested against every target: quantum cost 2^(128-20) queries = 2^126 gates < 2^128 \u2014 fails QPT-128. Fix: H(node, ladder_id, rung, level, index, l, r) as RFC 8554 (I, r) / XMSS-T do; zero bytes.",
  "untestable_assumptions": [
    "MM-SPR of the node hash (MTL Thm 2) \u2014 measured only at n \u2264 14 bits",
    "resolver behaviour above 1,232/1,400 B (fragmentation/TCP fallback) is from literature, not measured here",
    "the batch-reference RRSIG encoding (MTL-Type 2/3) is this audit's protocol decision, not an IETF draft"
  ]
